==English==
{{wikidata lexeme|L6319}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*seh₂-||*dʰeh₁-}}
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:satisfyen<ety:der<fro:satisfier>>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|satisfyen}}, {{m|enm|satisfien}}, from {{der|en|fro|satisfiier}}, {{m|fro|satisfier}} (also {{cog|fro|satisfaire}}), from {{der|en|la|satisfaciō|satisfacere}}, from {{m|la|satis||enough, sufficient}} + {{m|la|faciō||to make; to do}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsætɪsfaɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-satisfy.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyphenation|en|sat|is|fy}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To  be [[enough]] (for)
#: {{ux|en|That brief explanation will never '''satisfy'''.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[meet]] the needs of, to [[fulfill]] the wishes or [[requirement]]s of {{q|someone}}.
##: {{syn|en|fill}}
##: {{ux|en|The final rehearsal of the day seemed to '''satisfy''' the director.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[provide]] what is wanted or [[require]]d for {{q|something}}.
##: {{ux|en|Even three giant helpings of turkey and ham didn't '''satisfy''' her appetite.}}
##: {{syn|en|supply|appease|gratify}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=IX|passage=Death shall {{...}} with us two / Be forced to '''satisfy''' his ravenous maw.|year=1873}}
#* {{quote-song|en|author=w:Billy Joel|authorlabel=no|title=w:You May Be Right|album={{w|Glass Houses (album)|Glass Houses}}|date=7 March 1980|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ilsv0C1-aBw|text=Now think of all the years you tried to<br>Find someone to '''satisfy''' you<br>I might be as crazy as you say<br>If I'm crazy then it's true<br>That it's all because of you<br>And you wouldn't want me any other way}}
# {{lb|en|finance|transitive}} To [[pay]] to the extent of what is claimed or due.
#: {{ux|en|to '''satisfy''' a creditor}}
# {{lb|en|law|transitive}} To answer or discharge (a claim, debt, legal demand, etc.); to give compensation for.
#: {{ux|en|to '''satisfy''' a claim or an execution}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics|logic|transitive}} To cause (a sentence) to be true when the sentence is interpreted in one's universe.
#: {{ux|en|The complex numbers '''satisfy''' <math>\exists x:x^2+1=0</math>.}}
# {{lb|en|dated|literary|transitive}} To [[convince]] by [[ascertain]]ing; to free from doubt.
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|chapter=19|passage=I was resolved to '''satisfy''' myself whether this ragged Elijah was really dogging us or not, and with that intent crossed the way with Queequeg, and on that side of it retraced our steps.}}

